  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "Just one simulation might not be enough to know if you'll have enough pizza. But simulating the party 100 times will give you a better idea.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Define a variable to keep track of how many parties were “successful.” A successful party is one where there was enough pizza to feed everyone.\r\n2. For each simulation, if the number of slices you ordered (42) was enough to feed everyone, add 1 to the count of successful parties.\r\n3. Print how many successful parties there were out of 100.",
